#[chapter/06/lore]{
  notes: [
    "Bonk City's glass is made of old impacts — collisions melted down and forgiven into transparency. Its lanterns show light without claiming to be it."
    "Mr. BoonWAP debuts: a sentient pie of boonberries — berries a wish once passed over, each holding a drop of the granting. He serves himself in slices and is never smaller."
    "Asked what she would wish for, Boof cannot say. BoonWAP approves: a wish you can't say yet is still proofing."
    "Mr. BaneWAP shadows the city gates, lattice-crusted, keeping out of the light — and leaves ahead of Boof on the road to the oath stone."
    "The bonk-kiln melts the blow out of anything struck and pours it off as clear glass. Its keeper offered to forgive the egg's crack; Boof stepped wide of the tongs."
    "Dent-lanterns throw bright creases on the cobbles — streets the light remembers, some since moved. Chime-gutters ring in the rain so a roofer can hear which roof leaks; lamplighters' lamp..."
    "Glaziers etch # on a pane's street face (the face that travels) and . on its inside face (the face that stays); a pane hung backward shows you yourself. Pane-snails graze soot by night, a..."
    "A plaza stall sells brace-boxes: pocket weathers combined from two nouns, a sigil, and braces, written on the lid first so they can be checked and refused. They hold only what both nouns ..."
    "Glass over, never scrape — the glaziers' first law. A folio is never scraped to mend it: the new page is glassed over the old, and a child's thumbprint left on the glass goes under the pr..."
  ]
}

